concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-417 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "417 Saving provisions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-417 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this item under subsection 38ZC(1) of the Mutual Assistance in Criminal  Schedule 1  Main amendments  Matters Act 1987 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia. (2) A nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of this item under subsection 38ZC(2) of the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act 1987 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as a nomination in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia. (3) A thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate under the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act 1987 before the commencement of this item has effect, after that commencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, an eligible Federal Circuit Court Judge under that Act. National Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this item under subsection 38ZC(1) of the Mutual Assistance in Criminal  Schedule 1  Main amendments  Matters Act 1987 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia. (2) A nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of this item under subsection 38ZC(2) of the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act 1987 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as a nomination in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia. (3) A thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate under the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act 1987 before the commencement of this item has effect, after that commencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, an eligible Federal Circuit Court Judge under that Act. National Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b27639998960a05b574300f53000685fe42ca6e890e821ac81881b9c819623ca" ;
    cof:pageNumber "67"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Consent and nomination continue in force after commencement." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf> ;
    dc:source "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf, p.67" ;
    cml:asserts concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-417-norm .
