concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-514 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "514 Saving provisions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-514 ;
    values:originalText "(1) An appointment that is in force immediately before the commencement of this item under subsection 6DB(1) of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as an appointment in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia under that subsection. (2) A consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this item under subsection 6DB(2) of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia. (3) A thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate, as an issuing authority, under the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979 before the commencement of this item has effect, after that commencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, a Judge of  Main amendments  Schedule 1  the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as an issuing authority, under that Act. Tertiary Education Quality and Standards Agency Act 2011" ;
    skos:definition "(1) An appointment that is in force immediately before the commencement of this item under subsection 6DB(1) of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as an appointment in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia under that subsection. (2) A consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this item under subsection 6DB(2) of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia. (3) A thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate, as an issuing authority, under the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979 before the commencement of this item has effect, after that commencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, a Judge of  Main amendments  Schedule 1  the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as an issuing authority, under that Act. Tertiary Education Quality and Standards Agency Act 2011"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b1b46738cf140951882d3efbcaee894b19c46b3e9c13cba0c43cf30bdb354aaa" ;
    cof:pageNumber "80"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Continuation of appointments and consents" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf> ;
    dc:source "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf, p.80" ;
    cml:asserts concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-514-norm .
